			<title>Replying to Alon it’s always funny how people that say this never actually set out the numbers</title>
			<link>https://www.facebook.com/reel/1585254836932631/</link>
			<description>Replying to Alon it’s always funny how people that say this never actually set out the numbers. China has, at most, 500 actually up-and-running data centres, most of which are not hyperscale data centres like in the United States, whereas the United States has upwards of 5,500. The scale is astronomical. China is not competing with us on data centres but they are beating us at AI because one is treating it like a vanity project for oligarchs to get wealthier and one is treating it like a development in software&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
