		<item>
			<guid isPermaLink="false">277755958764636_122235190730352810</guid>
			<title>A good baseline for politics might be that if the IDF is doing it, maybe you shun it</title>
			<link>https://www.facebook.com/reel/1514218933888450/</link>
			<description>A good baseline for politics might be that if the IDF is doing it, maybe you shun it. This isn’t universal and of course the classic thing goes, “My enemy breathes too.” But if they’re saying that veterans are worth celebrating, consider why they think they’re worth celebrating. Consider what actual labour would go into changing both the actually existing social construction of that identity that they find worth celebrating and... What do we want to reclaim from it?&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
